From 96a76691dd36897deb5a95c3391bccbe883a361c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Mostovoy <stavultras@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 17:10:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 25/25] hw/arm/mt7981: MT7988A/D (Filogic 880 / 860)

mt7988-router: the MediaTek MT7988A (Filogic 880) and MT7988D (Filogic
860, the same die with cpu@3 disabled by the board's DT).  The official
OpenWrt chain runs unmodified: BL2 (DDR3/DDR4 calibration, also the
"comb" BL2s), BL31, U-Boot and Linux.

* target/arm: a cortex-a73 CPU model (the A72 model with the A73 MIDR and
  CPUACTLR_EL1 at its A73 encoding): TF-A for the MT7988 has only
  Cortex-A73 cpu_ops and errata code.
* RouterSoC: cpu_type, MCUCFG base (0x100e0000: secondary core boot
  addresses), xHCI base / IRQ (ssusb1 0x11200000, SPI 172); DRAM aliases
  up to base + 8 GB (U-Boot's get_ram_size probes that far).
* Built-in switch (gmac0=mt7988-switch): the MT7531 model's registers
  memory mapped at 0x15020000 (IRQ SPI 209), internal PHYs 0..3 via its
  PHY_IAC, modelled on the MT7981 SoC GbE PHY with the MT7988 ID
  (03a2:9481); internal 2.5G PHY with the MT7988 ID (0033:9c11).
* eFuse: GbE PHY calibration cells (0x940 + 0x14 * port), LVTS
  calibration for both LVTS controllers; LVTS controller at +0x100.
* Boot strap 0x1001f6f0 [11:10] (0 NOR, 1 SPI-NAND, 2 eMMC, 3 SNFI/SD):
  U-Boot sets /chosen/rootdisk from it.
* PWM channel blocks at 0x80 + 0x40 * n (like MT7981).
* LEDs: MediaTek PHY LED registers (mtk-phy-lib: VEND2 0x24..0x27, for
  the SoC GbE PHYs, MT7531 PHYs and the internal 2.5G PHYs; LED0 lights
  on link after reset) and the source swphy:PORT:N (a switch PHY's LED).

Checked: Asus ZenWiFi BT8 (MT7988D, SPI-NAND, FIP and Factory in UBI),
TP-Link TL-7DR7230 v1 (MT7988D, OpenWrt snapshot), Bananapi BPi-R4
(MT7988A, eMMC): LAN through the built-in switch, WAN on the 2.5G PHY,
USB 3.0, LEDs.

